<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:08:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>ASEAN offers Myanmar's sidelined leaders a path back to summits, but says restrictions will stay until there is meaningful progress on its peace plan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a7b3f7e2dfa5f0610415e7a17d8f0f9d60a80333eab9eb2741be76f29042c7a</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T12:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/asean-offers-myanmar-s-sidelined-leaders-a-path-back-to-summits-but-says-restrictions-will-stay-unti/a-79951878--8a50f9fda2bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/asean-offers-myanmar-s-sidelined-leaders-a-path-back-to-summits-but-says-restrictions-will-stay-until-there-is-meaningful-progress-on-its-peace-plan/a-79951878?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Southeast Asian leaders have agreed to engage Myanmar in stages after years of excluding its leaders from high-level meetings. The bloc says Myanmar could regain full representation if it makes progress on a peace plan.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Macron urges unity as Francophonie summit opens in Cambodia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a93e16d65dc9afdb5fc9f68a8357756dc0a91f0bd3b75ada1f6cdd3104c7af1</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-urges-unity-as-francophonie-summit-opens-in-cambodia/a-79951201--02576530ba13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-urges-unity-as-francophonie-summit-opens-in-cambodia/a-79951201?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leaders of French-speaking nations gathered in Phnom Penh as a row over who should lead the Francophonie and Congo’s threat to quit put pressure on Macron to broker consensus.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines wins first Eurovision Song Contest Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd40e1eab88a024202a7e20e7484c4415940becf09000aef27efa283dac86f2d</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T22:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-wins-first-eurovision-song-contest-asia/a-79950050--13c562f8bc59.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-wins-first-eurovision-song-contest-asia/a-79950050?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Eleven countries took part in the competition in Bangkok. Teenage winner Carmelle Collado's winning dance song is a tribute to Filipino women.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>New facilities in Laos and Cambodia: Is China expanding its military presence in Southeast Asia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f23084f70e15045c38c90d9620f3e48e3b151aa8b24fbffc3df3dd43fe5d921</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-facilities-in-laos-and-cambodia-is-china-expanding-its-military-presence-in-southeast-asia/a-79944798--c731be0f2b99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-facilities-in-laos-and-cambodia-is-china-expanding-its-military-presence-in-southeast-asia/a-79944798?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China has been growing its economic relationships in Southeast Asia. Now new military facilities in Laos and Cambodia are causing smaller countries to worry China's military networks are also expanding.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India: UK's Prince William, wife Kate to visit India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2b75ea296f1d21bc297bacf3824acdfc8f33a2e9672f104cea4e2ba9e5d45d4</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-uk-s-prince-william-wife-kate-to-visit-india/live-79946817--eea5b5bdc735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-uk-s-prince-william-wife-kate-to-visit-india/live-79946817?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During their trip to India, Prince William and Kate will attend the Earthshot Prize ceremony in Mumbai and other events linked to Indian cricket, fashion and cinema.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump to meet Xi, Putin for three-way huddle on nuclear arms talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6bbd1b357e214befa817ffeb9c6b1d31ee0584d40dd2f30dd0585263513c9f6d</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T04:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-to-meet-xi-putin-for-three-way-huddle-on-nuclear-arms-talks/a-79946408--68d06493f128.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-to-meet-xi-putin-for-three-way-huddle-on-nuclear-arms-talks/a-79946408?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The White House has said President Donald Trump will urge Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin to discuss cutting nuclear arsenals in Shenzhen next week, though a senior US official expects no agreement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Beijing faces Russia dilemma amid talk of Xi-Trump-Putin summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca2b14490249e0b6885f377f21b3b84b934bb41c3bcf7a4a1c35fe5b5326d5a5</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:08:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/beijing-faces-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427--7505a45629f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/beijing-faces-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China is forced to tread carefully as it considers hosting a meeting between Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin, and Donald Trump. While the optics are sure to favor Moscow, Beijing is risking its image on the global stage.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's wiretapping scandal opens a political fault line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5bed9d39a641447d13bd6b033b870dbee08c7a480dd54ce67069e74d3496d00</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-a-political-fault-line/a-79939753--0451bf449bfd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-a-political-fault-line/a-79939753?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senior police officers are accused of illegally monitoring President Prabowo Subianto, exposing rival networks within Indonesia's security establishment and renewing concerns about political misuse of surveillance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sri Lanka: Rights groups sound alarm over proposed anti-terror law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:838d0256d26b85dab86f4f07dfd2e1f2169da0120539fcd15cc74e9b2413b381</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-rights-groups-sound-alarm-over-proposed-anti-terror-law/a-79932227--abd4d2b11674.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-rights-groups-sound-alarm-over-proposed-anti-terror-law/a-79932227?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Sri Lankan government is looking to replace a controversial anti-terror law, but critics say the new one is just as bad.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Exiled journalists still repressed by regime</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89cacca9b340244bac27a114b3ab5b8734187b6eaa1891bc6dfae64d2e088aee</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694--82c71d3aa718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For many independent reporters, leaving Iran does not mean fully escaping the grasp of the Iranian state. The regime uses family members, bank accounts and the property they left behind to apply pressure across borders.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a8976e7225d3cca5c2d1db4ad1b2e63dba1698c9759cf1b99b3ab8bd6e1184c</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Megaspeed and the battle to go high-end Nvidia chips into China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67a282a6c876382ac014fc4bb5de449ee3b62b5d644c064c7a484fe75f4bd809</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129--5e400fbb45fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang's affair with a suspected Chinese spy has shone a light on Megaspeed, the company she worked for. It is under investigation in the US for smuggling Nvidia chips into China, which it denies.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>India's demonetization: 10 years on, economic benefits still disputed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dce68e99ebf9ea713ab693a8b88ea43d2a1b4e67651b0a14c66447fc41b5226</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-demonetization-10-years-on-economic-benefits-still-disputed/a-79903331--2fc450e61f09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-demonetization-10-years-on-economic-benefits-still-disputed/a-79903331?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A decade after the 2016 currency ban, its impact on India's economy and the fight against black money remains contested.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'No choice but to bear it': Delhi's unrelenting air pollution crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13585655ca57fd0a73bc41af6a3cb21b46e7bd0376c12a288b6df7fbb5a73b2c</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-choice-but-to-bear-it-delhi-s-unrelenting-air-pollution-crisis/a-79873124--aa42da1e16d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-choice-but-to-bear-it-delhi-s-unrelenting-air-pollution-crisis/a-79873124?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite years of government interventions, emergency restrictions and public outrage, Delhi continues to battle dangerously polluted air every winter. Why isn't there a lasting solution to a predictable crisis?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
